From 1594ed7b81c2301cfd1a2d78b104465a5f43bc42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Mandrigin <i@mandrigin.ru>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:10:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] =?UTF-8?q?local:=20attach=20mode=20=E2=80=94=20swap?=
 =?UTF-8?q?s=20run=20on=20long-standing=20chains?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LEZ_M3_ATTACH=1 attaches a swap run to standing labeled chains
(LEZ_ATTACH_BTC_RUN / LEZ_ATTACH_LEZ_RUN) instead of provisioning and
tearing down per-run chains: injectable child run ids, pre-existing
manifest validation, container-only inventory reconciliation, funding
discovery over unspent mature coinbases instead of virgin-height
assumptions, no mempool/tip freezes, persistent wallet identities
(LEZ_ATTACH_MAKER/TAKER_IDENTITY_DIR), one-time bootstrap reuse
(LEZ_ATTACH_BOOTSTRAP_MANIFEST), retained chains at cleanup with an
attach-aware attestation.
